# conf — configuration

This product wires `conf.Load()` + `conf.MustLoadAt[*AppConfig]("", "app")`.

- One `config.toml`; sections bind to typed structs via `conf.Section[T]("name")`
  (defaults → file → env → validate). Assembly-time values use
  `conf.MustLoadAt[T]("", "section")` in `Modules()`.
- Strict decode: an unknown key in a consumed section, or a whole section nothing
  consumes, fails boot with a did-you-mean. `conf.KnownSections("app")` silences
  sections read via LoadAt.
- Env overrides win: `ULTRA_<SECTION>_<FIELD>`. Durations are strings ("30s").
- `SetDefaults()` / `Validate() error` conventions on the struct.
- Hot reload: `conf.ReloadSection[T]("name")` gives a live handle — never cache
  `.Get()`; a bad edit keeps old values serving and turns /healthz unhealthy.
- `go run . config reference` prints the annotated config.

